```jsx
function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  const handleClick = () => {
    setCount(count + 1);
    setCount(count + 1);
    setCount(count + 1);
  };

  return <button onClick={handleClick}>{count}</button>;
}
```

questions.explanation:
All three `setCount` calls read the same stale `count` (0) from the closure. Each sets count to `0 + 1 = 1`. React 18 batches them into one re-render with count = 1. Use functional updates `setCount(c => c + 1)` three times to get 3.

## 📊 How It Works

![Batching and the update queue](/diagrams/react/batching_updates.svg)

