An empty dependency array `[]` tells React that the effect function has no dynamic dependencies and should only execute once after the component's initial mount (after the initial DOM paint). It will not re-run on subsequent re-renders because the dependency array never changes. Furthermore, if a cleanup function is returned, React will only run that cleanup once when the component unmounts from the DOM. (Note: in React 18 Strict Mode development, effects run mount -> unmount -> mount once to verify proper cleanup handling).

## 📊 How It Works

![The three dependency-array shapes](/diagrams/react/effect_deps_cleanup.svg)

