An uncontrolled component leaves the input's state in the DOM itself. Supplying `defaultValue` sets the initial value of the HTML `<input>` element on first mount, but subsequent keystrokes update the underlying DOM node without notifying or modifying any React state. React does not control the value over time. In contrast, a controlled component provides a `value` prop bound to React state and an `onChange` handler that updates state on every user keystroke, making React the single source of truth.

## 📊 How It Works

![Who holds the value](/diagrams/react/controlled_uncontrolled.svg)

