questions.explanation:
In React Context, consumers subscribe to the Provider's `value` prop as a whole. React does not provide built-in granular or selective field-level subscriptions. Whenever the value passed to `Provider` changes by reference (`Object.is(oldVal, newVal) === false`), React marks *every* component calling `useContext` for that context as requiring a re-render, regardless of which properties within the context object that specific component destructures. To avoid unnecessary re-renders, you can split contexts by responsibility, wrap children in `React.memo`, or use third-party state managers like Zustand.

